      trivia: "【The Scale of the Burning】The Cuban Davidoffs burnt at Basel in August 1989 are put at around 130,000, with estimates equating them to 9.8–15 million dollars at today’s retail values. Protest over quality, or theatre in a trademark war — the framing is contested still.\n【The World’s First Commercial Lancero】The Davidoff No. 1 of 1969 is held to be the first lancero ever offered for sale, identical in dimensions to the Cohiba Lancero. Relics of the Cuban era remain high-priced collectors’ items to this day.\n【The Signature on the Band】The cursive “Davidoff” of the white band is said to derive from Zino’s own signature — the name of the man they called the “King of Cigars”, made the very mark of quality assurance."
